194
00:24:49,000 --> 00:25:01,000
Archaeology preserves a tiny unfair sample of human behavior. Cannabis leaves decay. Smoke vanishes. Wooden pipes burn. Leather containers rot.

195
00:25:01,000 --> 00:25:10,000
camps disappear. Most people were not buried with 789 grams of botanical evidence and excellent desert drainage.

196
00:25:10,000 --> 00:25:19,000
The first users may have lived centuries or millennia earlier. They left no residue that survived. This is the central frustration. The chemical trace

197
00:25:19,000 --> 00:25:27,000
in abrasure marks the earliest moment we can confidently see, not the moment the idea was born. And the idea itself was

198
00:25:27,000 --> 00:25:36,000
larger than getting high. Humans discovered that one plant could become food, fiber, cord, cloth, oil, medicine,

199
00:25:36,000 --> 00:25:44,000
